From 7d5a864798738e15545430eee49586b27e965b01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:43:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): give paced headroom a one-run recovery
 floor

PACED at idle was an absorbing zero: floor(avg_running * factor) admitted nothing, so the next average stayed zero. Preserve one shared provider slot after deferrable scaling; HELD still admits none. Known quota walls already reroute before pacing, so govern the destination rather than treating ordinary pacing as a wall.

Proof: new recovery suite RED 9 failures on base; GREEN 63 tests across pacing, recovery and quota wall/release suites. Includes far-walled default reroute with destination pacing and occupied-floor rejection.
